# A project's own container downloads a stored file. ContainerFetch (a
# project-local infra node under nodes/container_fetch/) runs a tiny HTTP
# server in a container; its run asks for the file's container link and
# hands it to that server, which downloads it and answers how many bytes it
# got. The node starts with NO `file` set: the test writes one
# `@asset("assets/data.bin", Blob)` line, and asserts the count the
# container read equals the payload it wrote.

fetch = ContainerFetch

out = Debug
out.data = fetch.size
